---
import Banner from "../../components/Banner.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  pageId="legal"
  fullTitle="Legal: License, Privacy and Accessibility | Gephi"
  description="Gephi license, privacy and GDPR information, security policy and accessibility statement."
>
  <Banner containerClass="my-5 py-4">
    <h1>Legal</h1>
    <p class="fs-5 mb-1">
      Gephi is a community-driven open-source project. Its finances are held by our fiscal host, <a
        href="https://opencollective.com/gephi"
        class="fw-bold text-white">Open Collective</a
      >. Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@gephi.org" class="fw-bold text-white">contact@gephi.org</a>.
    </p>
  </Banner>

  <main class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 col-xl-8">
        <section id="license" class="mb-5">
          <h2>License</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Gephi Desktop</strong> is free, open-source software, dual-licensed under the <a
              href="https://opensource.org/licenses/CDDL-1.0">CDDL 1.0</a
            > and the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html">GNU General Public License v3</a>. Where a
            choice of GPL versions is offered, the project elects to use GPLv3 only. The full texts are in the
            <a href="https://github.com/gephi/gephi">source repository</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Gephi Lite</strong>, the web version, is free, open-source software under the <a
              href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html">GNU General Public License v3</a
            >. Its source code is in the <a href="https://github.com/gephi/gephi-lite">gephi-lite repository</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can use Gephi Desktop and Gephi Lite for commercial and non-commercial purposes at no cost, and build
            applications on top of the Gephi Toolkit without opening your own code. If you modify Gephi's own source
            files and distribute the result, you must publish those changes under the same license terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="privacy" class="mb-5">
          <h2>Privacy and GDPR</h2>
          <h3 class="h5">This website</h3>
          <p>
            gephi.org does not use cookies or JavaScript trackers. To measure visits, we use a Matomo tracking pixel
            hosted by <a href="https://www.ouestware.com/">OuestWare</a>, which collects page, browser, referrer, and IP
            address data (with IP addresses anonymized by truncating the last two bytes).
          </p>
          <h3 class="h5">Gephi Lite</h3>
          <p>
            Gephi Lite runs in your browser. The graphs you open are processed locally and are not uploaded to our
            servers. Your preferences and, if you connect, your GitHub session are stored in your browser's local
            storage. To measure visits, we use a Matomo tracking pixel hosted by <a href="https://www.ouestware.com/"
              >OuestWare</a
            >, which collects page, browser, referrer, and IP address data (with IP addresses anonymized by truncating
            the last two bytes).
          </p>
          <p>
            Signing in with GitHub is optional. It lets you save and open graphs in your own GitHub Gists, with requests
            relayed through a proxy to work around browser restrictions. Gephi Lite does not send crash reports.
          </p>
          <h3 class="h5">Gephi Desktop</h3>
          <p>
            Gephi runs entirely on your computer and does not send your data anywhere. The one exception is error
            reporting: when Gephi encounters an error, it can send a report to our Sentry account. Reports contain
            application logs only, with personal information such as the username removed. Sending reports is optional,
            and all tracking can be disabled in Gephi's Settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="security" class="mb-5">
          <h2>Security</h2>
          <p>
            Gephi Desktop only works with local files and does not connect to the web, apart from optional crash
            reporting. Gephi Lite runs in your browser and keeps your graphs on your device. Our <a
              href="https://github.com/gephi/gephi/blob/master/SECURITY.md">security policy</a
            > covers supported versions, how releases are secured and plugin safety.
          </p>
          <p>
            To report a vulnerability in Gephi Desktop or Gephi Lite, email <a href="mailto:contact@gephi.org"
              >contact@gephi.org</a
            >. For Gephi Desktop you can also <a href="https://github.com/gephi/gephi/security/advisories/new"
              >report it privately on GitHub</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="accessibility" class="mb-5">
          <h2>Accessibility</h2>
          <p>Our accessibility conformance report (VPAT) will be published here.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="disclaimer" class="mb-5">
          <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>
            Gephi Desktop, Gephi Lite and the content of this website are provided "as is", without warranty of any
            kind. We aim for accuracy but cannot guarantee it. We are not responsible for the content of third-party
            sites we link to.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
